The fresh A5 mutation built successfully, then failed for the intended reason: K reached `<k> true` for `[0,0]` while the mutated target demanded `false`, producing `WarnStuckClaimState` and exit 1. I’m adding one separate body-sensitivity probe so the real-program pinning is evidenced independently of the result mutation: a function body changed to return `false` must not prove an empty-list `true` target.
apply patch
